From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Myles Liu <lyx981mike@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:43:39 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] qualcommax: ipq807x: use the CPU's AES instructions in the
 kernel

The Cortex-A53 cores have the ARMv8 Crypto Extensions, but the kernel was
built without the drivers that use them, so kernel AES ran as generic C.
Measured on an MX4300 (1424-byte buffers, one core): AES-CBC 0.45 Gbit/s
generic vs 9.1 Gbit/s with the extensions; AES-GCM 6.0 Gbit/s and
AES-CBC + HMAC-SHA256 3.3 Gbit/s. Used by the kernel's own crypto users
(IPsec, WPA3 management frame protection, dm-crypt, ...).
---
 target/linux/qualcommax/ipq807x/config-default | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq807x/config-default b/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq807x/config-default
index 66d44a56b1..dbc0ad7281 100644
--- a/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq807x/config-default
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq807x/config-default
@@ -1,6 +1,10 @@
 CONFIG_AQUANTIA_PHY=y
 CONFIG_ARM_PSCI_CPUIDLE_DOMAIN=y
 CONFIG_CRC_ITU_T=y
+CONFIG_CRYPTO_AES_ARM64_CE=y
+CONFIG_CRYPTO_AES_ARM64_CE_BLK=y
+CONFIG_CRYPTO_AES_ARM64_CE_CCM=y
+CONFIG_CRYPTO_GHASH_ARM64_CE=y
 CONFIG_DT_IDLE_GENPD=y
 CONFIG_IPQ_CMN_PLL=y
 CONFIG_IPQ_GCC_8074=y
-- 
2.56.1

